    "obligations": [
      "Unit defining sections and the area-square-one Fubini--Study normalization give integral -3/2.",
      "Summability and decreasing convergence give a common lower bound and a canonical L1 limit.",
      "Distributional convergence gives the finite closed current S and strict residual R.",
      "The tail remains quasi-psh under each proper modification and is finite off the exceptional locus.",
      "Gauduchon trace pairing includes every compact smooth surface model, without projectivity of the given model.",
      "Each divisor has strictly positive Gauduchon area and tail generic coefficients vanish at most linearly in tail mass.",
      "Finite Lelong additivity and the tail bound identify the convergent full profile.",
      "Profile-to-ideal implication uses the projective primary theorem only in common closed integer C*kappa on Kahler P2.",
      "Further point blowups on projective models recover point Lelong numbers from generic divisor coefficients.",
      "Equality of profile and all-weight ideals is invariant under the common factor two in the Lelong convention.",
      "Reverse implication on arbitrary compact modifications uses the already established birational ideal-order theorem.",
      "The known countable divisorial-envelope theorem identifies q~u; no new Choquet proof is duplicated.",
      "Strict R proves bigness, and a closed majorant bounds masses for every Hermitian background on P2.",
      "For every ordinary representative w~q~u, divisorial removal gives a positive closed bounded-potential residual K.",
      "Bounded residual trace measures charge no pluripolar set, so degree-one non-pluripolar T equals K.",
      "Stokes with any smooth dd^c-closed L computes the mixed degree-one correction.",
      "Finite divisor partial sums have explicitly computed closed top mass.",
      "Only the closed case of existing singularity-volume monotonicity is used for the upper bound.",
      "Local bounded truncations of a psh potential of S give the smooth top-product lower bound without assuming a small unbounded locus.",
      "Closed ordinary-type invariance transfers the closed top mass from u to every w.",
      "The identical canonical strict superlevels in both backgrounds give the Borel signed-correction identity.",
      "All signed correction terms have finite variation before integration; no nonclosed unbounded mass invariance is assumed.",
      "R>0 makes the common actual mass strictly positive; both extremal volumes follow because every representative is covered.",
      "The cutoff form tau is real, dd^c-closed and has the stated nonzero exterior derivative.",
      "The summable geometric coefficients have A=1/4 and yield R>=kappa/4, hence both volumes at least 1/16.",
      "The Vandermonde determinant excludes a single pencil and infinite positive prime coefficients exclude analytic ideal types."
